course: dictionary
lesson: 13989
title: Longer: more length, more time, or not any more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Longer is a word for comparing. It means having more length than something else, or lasting for more time. «The pencil is longer than the rubber.» The pencil has more length, so it is the bigger of the two.
explain: Look at the words around longer for clues. Than tells you what is being compared. Without than, you compare with the thing just before. «My rope is short, but yours is longer» means yours has more length than my rope.
explain: Longer can mean more time too. «Stay a little longer» means stay for a bit more time. Watch the small word no. «He no longer lives here» means he does not live here any more. When you see no longer, swap in «not any more» and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Longer is the comparing form of long.
fact: «Longer than» means more length or more time than something else.
fact: «No longer» means not any more.
fact: «A little longer» means a bit more time or a bit more length.
fact: «How much longer?» asks how big the difference is.
exercise: «The river is longer than the stream.» Which small word shows what the river is being compared with? | *than | river | the | is
exercise: «Stay a little longer, please.» What does longer mean here? | *More time | Shorter | Less fun | More colour, like a bright paint
exercise: «He no longer lives here.» What does this mean? | He lives here for a long time | He moved here yesterday | *He does not live here any more | He will move here next year
test: «She no longer plays football.» What does this mean? | She is very good at football | She plays football for a longer time | She plays football more than ever | *She does not play football any more
test: «My snake is longer than your snake.» Which snake has more length? | Both snakes are the same length | Your snake | *My snake | Neither snake has any length
exam: Which word completes «The snake is ___ than the worm.»? | short | *longer | happy | sad
